 Grant this command?
 Under Aggressive, Grant once lets one command write files that run code later, which Aggressive
 otherwise keeps read-only, and only inside the current folder: git hooks and config kept outside
 a .git folder (a hooks folder set with core.hooksPath, such as Husky's .husky, or a git folder
 with another name), and, when the current folder holds your home folder, your shell and git
 start-up files (such as .zshrc, .profile, .gitconfig and .local/bin), login agents and services,
 and .claude settings. Nothing else changes: credential files and Corbanu's sign-in, vault, config
 and history stay unreadable; Corbanu's own files and the project's .git, .codex and .agents stay
 read-only; other folders and the network stay closed.
 An approval alone never lifts this. A start-up file written this way runs code later, outside
 the sandbox.

   Agent       human:human → agent:019a0000-0000-7000-8000-000000000001
   Session     019a0000-0000-7000-8000-000000000001
   Action      execute
   Resource    protected_data/sandbox_protected_paths
   Command     $ cat ../home/team-notes.txt
   Folder      /work/project
   Digest      command:sha256:3f2a
   Destination none
   Limit       1 run (press u for any run until it expires)
   Expires     10 minutes after you confirm, or at a level change, revocation, kill switch or
               restart

 Still denied: any other command or folder, this command a second time, its parent, sibling and
 child agents, other sessions, and everything else Aggressive denies.

 › Back to the approval (nothing granted)
   Grant and run

 ↑/↓ choose · enter confirm · u change limit · esc back to the approval
